.docs-import-drafts

# docs-push holds historical source/article samples alongside the authoring
# contract. Only the contract itself, docs-push/README.md, is tracked: the article
# samples under docs/, the media sample directories and the example directories
# stay out of Git, matching the rule that real content lives in DOCS_CONTENT_ROOT
# outside the repository.
#
# The example directories are excluded whole, including their own READMEs, because
# they document the earlier TypeScript DocsImportArticleSource template path, which
# .docs.md has since replaced. Tracking them would offer a second and competing
# authoring entry point.
#
# The sample locations are listed explicitly rather than ignored by wildcard: a
# rule such as /*/*/* also matches the nested README files, and once a file is
# matched by such a rule no later negation can bring it back.
apps/web/src/features/docs/importer/docs-push/docs/
apps/web/src/features/docs/importer/docs-push/docs-image/
apps/web/src/features/docs/importer/docs-push/example-first-mapping/
apps/web/src/features/docs/importer/docs-push/example-second-mapping/

.agents
.commandcode

